==English==
{{was wotd|2007|December|5}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|inevitable|ly}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|US}} {{IPA|en|/ɪˈnɛvɪtəbli/|/ɪˈnɛvətəbli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-inevitably.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-inevitably.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# In a manner that is [[impossible]] to [[avoid]] or [[prevent]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Inevitably''', all creatures eventually die.}}
#: {{ux|en|The sun '''inevitably''' rises.}}
#: {{ux|en|Despite the town's best efforts, the dam '''inevitably''' gave way.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''inevitably''' cold winter approaches.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=June|title=Diesel locomotive operation on the Great Eastern Line|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=374|text=In a period of transition from steam to diesel, many of the schemes are '''inevitably''' of an interim nature and only on full dieselisation will the final pattern be determined and full benefit derived.}}
# As [[usual]]; [[predictably]]; as [[expected]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Inevitably''', the next-door neighbour began to mow his lawn just as she lays down her head after a long night shift.}}
#: {{ux|en|The child '''inevitably''' began to cry when his mother went to work.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''inevitably''' long line of customers queued for the latest 'Harry Potter'.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|in a manner that is impossible to avoid}} {{l|en|certainly}}, {{l|en|inexorably}}, {{l|en|unavoidably}}, {{l|en|necessarily}}
